#import "../template.typ": somatic_page

// PAGE 4: HOW TO USE THIS JOURNAL
// Authoritative tone, sophisticated vocabulary, structured guidance

#somatic_page(
  title: "A Gentler Approach",
  body_text: [
    #rect(fill: rgb("#F5F5F0"), stroke: 0.5pt + gray, inset: 15pt, radius: 2pt)[
      Traditional shadow work fails because it operates from the neck up. You are taught to *think* about your trauma, to *analyze* your patterns, to *understand* your wounds. But the shadow does not live in your thoughts—it lives in your *nervous system*. It is stored in the tightness of your jaw, the knot in your belly, the familiar pull toward self-destruction that your mind cannot explain but your body enacts automatically.
      
      This is why insight without embodiment is entertainment. You can understand your shadow for years and still be controlled by it. True integration requires *somatic awareness*—the ability to feel what you have learned to think away. The vagus nerve, the fascia, the gut-brain axis: these are the keepers of your shadow's memory. When you engage them, you do not merely *know* your shadow—you *liberate* it.
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    #align(center)[
      ◈ · ✦ · ◈
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    *How to Use This Journal:*
    
    1. *Do not rush.* Shadow work is not productive. It is *alchemical*. One page may take ten minutes or ten days. Trust the pace your body requires.
    
    2. *Honor resistance.* If a page feels "too much," put it down. This is not avoidance—it is discernment. Your nervous system knows when it is safe to dig deeper.
    
    3. *Write with your body, not your brain.* When a prompt asks, _"Where do you feel this?"_—stop thinking and *scan*. Place your hand on the sensation. Breathe into it. Write from there.
    
    4. *Repeat exercises.* The shadow reveals itself in layers. Returning to a page weeks later will unlock insights you were not ready to see the first time.
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    This journal follows a structured arc: Foundation → Excavation → Integration. Each phase builds upon the last. Do not skip ahead. The shadow rewards patience, not urgency.
  ],
  image_path: none,
  layout_style: "bottom"
)
